ACCEPTANCE BASELINE
===================
HLS-C001 bootstrap acceptance criteria:
1. Shared human + machine task registry exists.
2. Role declaration, heartbeat, visitor, decision, audit, and bootstrap tracking channels exist.
3. handoff.md starts with visitor issue and machine-readable coordination metadata.
4. Coordinator records role roster, assignments, priorities, acceptance criteria, and route changes here.
5. Worker task history exists under docs/worker-logs/.
6. Collaboration architecture + release-security roadmap exist under docs/architecture/.
7. With one active worker identity, at least six prioritized unfinished tasks remain available/planned.
8. Bootstrap is delivered by branch/commits/PR and independently audited before merge.

HLS-C002 PR #38 audit acceptance criteria:
1. Exact-SHA push-run semantics independently verified.
2. Security workflow path-filter behavior cannot deadlock formal release.
3. PowerShell 5.1/7 validation and all PR workflows pass.
4. Stale/wrong-event security runs cannot satisfy formal-release checks.
5. Audit queue records PASS/FAIL evidence.

ROLE ROSTER
===========
C0 | coordinator | global | active | coordination/bootstrap-v1
A0 | auditor     | global | active | logical independent review role held by same ChatGPT during bootstrap
W0 | worker      | HLS-C001 | active | coordination/bootstrap-v1

When new ChatGPT participants join, assign stable IDs (W1, W2, ... / A1 ...), require declaration in issue #40, and update handoff.md + tasks.json + this log.

